{"3789690": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "The Great Serpent Beholds", "steam_appid": 3789690, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The chief is dead. The pyre is lit. The oath is already sworn.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The Great Serpent Beholds</i> is a first-person mythological RPG. The dark seam where Norse and Slavic myth bleed into each other — a saga of vengeance, kinship, and the buried voices that refuse to stay silent.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the funeral of the warlord Grimnir, his sons Sigurd and Arnthor reject the elder Farlaf's counsel of harvest and peace. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>First-person combat</strong> with sword, spear, axe, archery and shield — close, heavy, and meant to be felt</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A homeland to walk back into:</strong> drowned shorelines, ancestral barrows, river-cut valleys, and the cave-paths beneath the world</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A branching saga</strong>, the brothers' road do not lead to the same ending</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Speak with the dead.</strong> The mounds of your forebears have things to say to anyone willing to listen at the right hour</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A mythology older than either tradition it draws from</strong> — gods, Norns, einherjar, and serpents braided into something its own</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skaldic-cadence writing</strong>, bone-flute, and choral verse</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you be the warrior the funeral fire demanded? Or will you hear what is still crawling, slow and patient, out of the mountain?</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The chief is dead. The pyre is lit. The oath is already sworn.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>The Great Serpent Beholds</i> is a first-person mythological RPG. The dark seam where Norse and Slavic myth bleed into each other — a saga of vengeance, kinship, and the buried voices that refuse to stay silent.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the funeral of the warlord Grimnir, his sons Sigurd and Arnthor reject the elder Farlaf's counsel of harvest and peace. </p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>First-person combat</strong> with sword, spear, axe, archery and shield — close, heavy, and meant to be felt</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A homeland to walk back into:</strong> drowned shorelines, ancestral barrows, river-cut valleys, and the cave-paths beneath the world</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A branching saga</strong>, the brothers' road do not lead to the same ending</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Speak with the dead.</strong> The mounds of your forebears have things to say to anyone willing to listen at the right hour</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A mythology older than either tradition it draws from</strong> — gods, Norns, einherjar, and serpents braided into something its own</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Skaldic-cadence writing</strong>, bone-flute, and choral verse</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you be the warrior the funeral fire demanded? Or will you hear what is still crawling, slow and patient, out of the mountain?</p>", "short_description": "A first-person mythological RPG of vengeance, prophecy, and the cold weight of fate. Sigurd and Arnthor, sons of a fallen chief, sail home to settle a blood debt — but the Norns have already woven a darker thread, and beneath the stone of the old country, the Great Serpent is shedding his skin.", "supported_languages": "English<strong>*</strong>, Russian<strong>*</strong><br><strong>*</strong>languages with full audio support", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.